{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceTraces","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTraceOnHecke","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH3Characters","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH3BlockRep","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH3BlockCharacter","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":90,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi21Reduced_ratio_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi21Reduced_ratio_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":818,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L818-L825","doc":"**Mixed-Symmetry `(2,1)` Nucleon Sector Ratio at the Classical Limit `q = 1`**:\nWhen projected onto the physical `I = 1/2` mixed-symmetry nucleon idempotent `e_{(2,1)}`\n(removing the `O(1)` symmetric `(3)` decuplet background), the neutron-to-proton amplitude\nratio at `q = 1` is `4 / 3 > 1` (`3 · χ̃_{(2,1)}(n)|_{q=1} = 4 · χ̃_{(2,1)}(p)|_{q=1}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.four_mul_chi21ReducedNeutron_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.four_mul_chi21ReducedNeutron_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":807,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L807-L816","doc":"Classical anchor value of the reduced `(2,1)` neutron amplitude at `q = 1`:\n`4 · χ̃_{(2,1)}(n)|_{q=1} = -8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.four_mul_chi21ReducedProton_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.four_mul_chi21ReducedProton_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":796,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L796-L805","doc":"Classical anchor value of the reduced `(2,1)` proton amplitude at `q = 1`:\n`4 · χ̃_{(2,1)}(p)|_{q=1} = -6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi21_neutron_eq_sub_sq_mul_reduced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi21_neutron_eq_sub_sq_mul_reduced","kind":"theorem","line":788,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L788-L794","doc":"Factorization `χ_{(2,1)}(n) = (q^2 - 1) · χ̃_{(2,1)}(n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi21_proton_eq_sub_sq_mul_reduced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi21_proton_eq_sub_sq_mul_reduced","kind":"theorem","line":780,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L780-L786","doc":"Factorization `χ_{(2,1)}(p) = (q^2 - 1) · χ̃_{(2,1)}(p)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi21ReducedNeutron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi21ReducedNeutron","kind":"def","line":774,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L774-L778","doc":"Desingularized mixed-symmetry `(2,1)` neutron amplitude `χ_{(2,1)}(n) / (q^2 - 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi21ReducedProton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi21ReducedProton","kind":"def","line":768,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L768-L772","doc":"Desingularized mixed-symmetry `(2,1)` proton amplitude `χ_{(2,1)}(p) / (q^2 - 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi21_neutronCoord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi21_neutronCoord","kind":"theorem","line":752,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L752-L766","doc":"**Mixed-Symmetry `(2,1)` Nucleon Sector on Neutron Word (Projected onto `e_{(2,1)}`)**:\nExact factored closed form of `χ_{(2,1)}(neutronCoord)` at `a = -(q - q⁻¹)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi21_protonCoord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi21_protonCoord","kind":"theorem","line":736,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L736-L750","doc":"**Mixed-Symmetry `(2,1)` Nucleon Sector on Proton Word (Projected onto `e_{(2,1)}`)**:\nExact factored closed form of `χ_{(2,1)}(protonCoord)` at `a = -(q - q⁻¹)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.tMod111_neutron_eq_q_sq_mul_proton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.tMod111_neutron_eq_q_sq_mul_proton","kind":"theorem","line":726,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L726-L734","doc":"**GPMT Renormalized Trace Ratio on the Killed `(1^3)` Sector**:\nUnder the Geer–Patureau-Mirand–Turaev renormalized trace `tMod111` on `H_3(q) e_{(1^3)}`,\nthe neutron observable is `q^2` times the proton observable (`t_D(n) / t_D(p) = q^{+2} > 1`\nfor `q > 1`, the exact inverse of the `(3)` decuplet ratio!). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi111_neutronCoord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi111_neutronCoord","kind":"theorem","line":712,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L712-L724","doc":"**Antisymmetric `(1^3)` Sector on Neutron Word**:\nAt `a = -(q - q⁻¹)/2`, `χ_{(1^3)}(neutronCoord) = -(q^2 + 1)^2 / (4 q^3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi111_protonCoord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi111_protonCoord","kind":"theorem","line":698,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L698-L710","doc":"**Antisymmetric `(1^3)` Sector on Proton Word**:\nAt `a = -(q - q⁻¹)/2`, `χ_{(1^3)}(protonCoord) = -(q^2 + 1)^2 / (4 q^5)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi3_proton_eq_q_sq_mul_neutron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi3_proton_eq_q_sq_mul_neutron","kind":"theorem","line":689,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L689-L696","doc":"**Symmetric `(3)` Sector Ratio**:\nIn the unphysical `I = 3/2` decuplet sector `(3)`, the proton character is `q^2` times the\nneutron character (`χ_{(3)}(n) / χ_{(3)}(p) = q^{-2} < 1` for `q > 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi3_neutronCoord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi3_neutronCoord","kind":"theorem","line":675,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L675-L687","doc":"**Symmetric `(3)` Decuplet Sector on Neutron Word**:\nAt `a = -(q - q⁻¹)/2`, `χ_{(3)}(neutronCoord) = (q^2 + 1)^2 / (4 q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi3_protonCoord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi3_protonCoord","kind":"theorem","line":661,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L661-L673","doc":"**Symmetric `(3)` Decuplet Sector on Proton Word**:\nAt `a = -(q - q⁻¹)/2`, `χ_{(3)}(protonCoord) = q (q^2 + 1)^2 / 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.neutronWord_foldl_eq_neutronCoord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.neutronWord_foldl_eq_neutronCoord","kind":"theorem","line":620,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L620-L659","doc":"**Exact Word-Fold Bridge for the Neutron Word**:\n`neutronCoord h a` is identically the `nfStep` fold of the production neutron word\n`neutronWord h a` from the identity coordinate vector `![1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.protonWord_foldl_eq_protonCoord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.protonWord_foldl_eq_protonCoord","kind":"theorem","line":578,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L578-L617","doc":"**Exact Word-Fold Bridge for the Proton Word**:\n`protonCoord h a` is identically the `nfStep` fold of the production proton word\n`protonWord h a` from the identity coordinate vector `![1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.vec6_ext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.vec6_ext","kind":"theorem","line":571,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L571-L575","doc":"Componentwise equality of six-vectors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.nfStep_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.nfStep_one","kind":"theorem","line":563,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L563-L568","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.nfStep_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.nfStep_zero","kind":"theorem","line":556,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L556-L561","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.neutronWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.neutronWord","kind":"def","line":549,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L549-L554","doc":"The production neutron word (`intra_order = \"borromean\"`, matching\n`QOU.Mass.NucleonWordTraceClosedForm.neutronWord`):\n`σ₀ σ₁⁻¹ σ₀ σ₁⁻¹ σ₀ σ₁⁻¹ (σ₀+a) (σ₀+a) σ₁⁻¹ σ₀ σ₀` with `σ⁻¹ = σ - h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.protonWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.protonWord","kind":"def","line":542,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L542-L547","doc":"The production proton word (`intra_order = \"borromean\"`, matching\n`QOU.Mass.NucleonWordTraceClosedForm.protonWord`):\n`σ₀ σ₁⁻¹ σ₀ σ₁⁻¹ σ₀ σ₁⁻¹ σ₀ (σ₀+a) (σ₁+a) σ₀ σ₀` with `σ⁻¹ = σ - h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.nfStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.nfStep","kind":"def","line":536,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L536-L540","doc":"One affine letter `(i, s, b) ↦ s • 1 + b • σ_i`, `i ≤ 1`, acting on `H_3(q)` normal-form\ncoordinates via `QOU.Machinery.H3.mulσ₀` and `mulσ₁`\n(matching `QOU.Mass.NucleonWordTraceClosedForm.nfStep`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.neutronCoord_5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.neutronCoord_5","kind":"theorem","line":532,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L532-L534","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.protonCoord_5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.protonCoord_5","kind":"theorem","line":528,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L528-L530","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.neutronCoord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.neutronCoord","kind":"def","line":515,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L515-L526","doc":"Normal-form coordinate vector of the production neutron word\n`σ₀ σ₁⁻¹ σ₀ σ₁⁻¹ σ₀ σ₁⁻¹ (σ₀+a) (σ₀+a) σ₁⁻¹ σ₀ σ₀`\n(matching step `s10` of `QOU.Mass.NucleonWordTraceClosedForm.neutronCoord`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.protonCoord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.protonCoord","kind":"def","line":503,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L503-L513","doc":"Normal-form coordinate vector of the production proton word\n`σ₀ σ₁⁻¹ σ₀ σ₁⁻¹ σ₀ σ₁⁻¹ σ₀ (σ₀+a) (σ₁+a) σ₀ σ₀`\n(matching step `s10` of `QOU.Mass.NucleonWordTraceClosedForm.protonCoord`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.tMod111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.tMod111","kind":"def","line":489,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L489-L493","doc":"The Geer–Patureau-Mirand–Turaev renormalized trace `t_D` on the `(1^3)` ideal\n([geer-patureau-mirand-turaev-2009] Theorem 3 & Corollary 17):\n`tMod111 q v = d_D(S^{(1^3)}) · χ_{(1^3)}(v)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.dMod111_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.dMod111_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":482,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L482-L487","doc":"The GPMT modified quantum dimension `dMod111 q` is non-vanishing for all `q ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.w111_slope_at_zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.w111_slope_at_zD","kind":"theorem","line":473,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L473-L480","doc":"The regular factor of `w_{(1^3)}(q, z) / (z - z_D)` evaluated at `z = z_D` equals `dMod111 q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.dMod111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.dMod111","kind":"def","line":468,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L468-L471","doc":"The Geer–Patureau-Mirand–Turaev modified quantum dimension `d_D(S^{(1^3)}) = w'_{(1^3)}(z_D)`\nof the killed `(1^3)` sector at Convention D. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.w111_factor_zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.w111_factor_zD","kind":"theorem","line":457,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L457-L466","doc":"**Geer–Patureau-Mirand–Turaev First-Order Factorization of `w_{(1^3)}(q, z)`**\n([geer-patureau-mirand-turaev-2009] / [geer-patureau-mirand-turaev-2013] Lemma 16 & Corollary 17):\n`w_{(1^3)}(q, z)` factors as `(z - z_D)` times the regular factor `q^2 (z - q) / (q^4 + q^2 + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.trM_conventionD_eq_twoRow_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.trM_conventionD_eq_twoRow_sum","kind":"theorem","line":447,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L447-L455","doc":"**Convention-D Wedderburn Decomposition of `trM`**:\nAt `z = z_D`, the `(1^3)` sector is killed and `trM` reduces to the two-row sum over `(3)` and `(2,1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.weights_conventionD_sum_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.weights_conventionD_sum_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":439,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L439-L445","doc":"At Convention D, the Markov weights satisfy `w_{(3)}(z_D) + 2 w_{(2,1)}(z_D) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.w111_conventionD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.w111_conventionD","kind":"theorem","line":431,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L431-L437","doc":"At Convention D, the antisymmetric `(1^3)` weight vanishes identically: `w_{(1^3)}(z_D) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.w21_conventionD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.w21_conventionD","kind":"theorem","line":420,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L420-L429","doc":"At Convention D, the mixed-symmetry `(2,1)` nucleon weight is `q^2 / (q^2 + 1)^2 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.w3_conventionD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.w3_conventionD","kind":"theorem","line":409,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L409-L418","doc":"At Convention D, the symmetric `(3)` weight is `(q^4 + 1) / (q^2 + 1)^2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.zD","kind":"def","line":406,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L406-L407","doc":"The canonical Convention-D Markov parameter `z_D = q^3 / (q^2 + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.trM_eq_wedderburn_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.trM_eq_wedderburn_sum","kind":"theorem","line":387,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L387-L404","doc":"**General Wedderburn character decomposition of the Markov trace on `H_3(q)`**:\nFor every normal-form vector `v : Fin 6 → K` and every Markov parameter `z : K`,\n`trM z (q - q⁻¹) v = w_{(3)}(q,z) χ_{(3)}(v) + w_{(2,1)}(q,z) χ_{(2,1)}(v) + w_{(1^3)}(q,z) χ_{(1^3)}(v)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.trM_eq_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.trM_eq_closed","kind":"theorem","line":378,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L378-L385","doc":"Closed linear formula for `trM z h v` expanding all 6 normal-form coordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.w111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.w111","kind":"def","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L374-L376","doc":"General Ocneanu/Wedderburn weight `w_{(1^3)}(q, z)` of the antisymmetric `(1^3)` sector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.w21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.w21","kind":"def","line":370,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L370-L372","doc":"General Ocneanu/Wedderburn weight `w_{(2,1)}(q, z)` of the mixed-symmetry `(2,1)` nucleon sector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.w3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.w3","kind":"def","line":366,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L366-L368","doc":"General Ocneanu/Wedderburn weight `w_{(3)}(q, z)` of the symmetric `(3)` sector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi111","kind":"def","line":363,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L363-L364","doc":"Antisymmetric `(1^3)` character on `H_3(q)` normal-form vectors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi21","kind":"def","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L360-L361","doc":"Mixed-symmetry `(2,1)` nucleon character on `H_3(q)` normal-form vectors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi3","kind":"def","line":357,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L357-L358","doc":"Symmetric `(3)` character on `H_3(q)` normal-form vectors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.blockOf_murphySum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.blockOf_murphySum","kind":"theorem","line":340,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L340-L347","doc":"Jucys–Murphy content sum action on the 2D `(2,1)` block ([aiston-morton-1997] Theorem 5.7):\n`blockOf q M = (q - q⁻¹) • I_2` (`m_{(2,1)} = q[1]_q + q⁻¹[-1]_q = q - q⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi111_murphySum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi111_murphySum","kind":"theorem","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L333-L338","doc":"Jucys–Murphy content sum eigenvalue on `(1^3)` ([aiston-morton-1997] Theorem 5.7):\n`m_{(1^3)} = q⁻¹[-1]_q + q^{-2}[-2]_q = -q⁻¹^3 - 2q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi3_murphySum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi3_murphySum","kind":"theorem","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L326-L331","doc":"Jucys–Murphy content sum eigenvalue on `(3)` ([aiston-morton-1997] Theorem 5.7):\n`m_{(3)} = q[1]_q + q^2[2]_q = q^3 + 2q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi21_fullTwist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi21_fullTwist","kind":"theorem","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L319-L324","doc":"Full-twist character on the 2D mixed-symmetry `(2,1)` block: `χ_{(2,1)}(Δ_3^2) = 2 · q^0 = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.blockOf_fullTwist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.blockOf_fullTwist","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L309-L317","doc":"Full-twist framing action on the 2D mixed-symmetry `(2,1)` block ([aiston-morton-1997] Theorem 5.5):\n`blockOf q (Δ_3^2) = 1 = q^0 · I_2` (`n_{(2,1)} = 2(0 + 1 - 1) = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chiM_eq_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chiM_eq_closed","kind":"theorem","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L298-L307","doc":"Closed linear form of the 2-dimensional `(2,1)` character `chiM q v`:\n`χ_{(2,1)}(v) = 2 v_0 + (q - q⁻¹)(v_1 + v_2) - v_3 - v_4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi111_fullTwist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi111_fullTwist","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L289-L296","doc":"Full-twist framing eigenvalue on the antisymmetric `(1^3)` block ([aiston-morton-1997] Theorem 5.5):\n`χ_{(1^3)}(Δ_3^2) = (q⁻¹)^6` (`n_{(1^3)} = 2(0 - 1 - 2) = -6`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi111_w0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi111_w0","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L285-L287","doc":"Half-twist eigenvalue on the antisymmetric `(1^3)` block: `χ_{(1^3)}(w_0) = (-q⁻¹)^3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi3_fullTwist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi3_fullTwist","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L276-L283","doc":"Full-twist framing eigenvalue on the symmetric `(3)` block ([aiston-morton-1997] Theorem 5.5):\n`χ_{(3)}(Δ_3^2) = q^6` (`n_{(3)} = 2(0 + 1 + 2) = 6`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi3_w0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.chi3_w0","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L272-L274","doc":"Half-twist eigenvalue on the symmetric `(3)` block: `χ_{(3)}(w_0) = q^3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.murphySumNF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.murphySumNF","kind":"def","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L268-L270","doc":"The total additive Jucys–Murphy content sum `M = M(1) + M(2) + M(3) = σ_0 + σ_1 + σ_0 σ_1 σ_0 ∈ Z(H_3(q))`\n([aiston-morton-1997] Theorem 5.7). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.murphy3NF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.murphy3NF","kind":"def","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L264-L266","doc":"The third additive Jucys–Murphy element `M(3) = σ_1 σ_0 σ_1⁻¹ + h σ_1 = σ_1 + σ_0 σ_1 σ_0`\nsatisfying `(q - q⁻¹) M(3) = σ_1 σ_0^2 σ_1 - 1` in `H_3(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.murphy2NF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.murphy2NF","kind":"def","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L261-L262","doc":"The second additive Jucys–Murphy element `M(2) = σ_0` in `H_3(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.fullTwistNF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.fullTwistNF","kind":"def","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L258-L259","doc":"The full-twist framing element `Δ_3^2 = w_0^2 = (σ_0 σ_1 σ_0)^2` in `H_3(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.w0NF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.w0NF","kind":"def","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L254-L256","doc":"The longest element `w_0 = σ_0 σ_1 σ_0` in the 6-element normal-form basis\n`[1, σ_0, σ_1, σ_1 σ_0, σ_0 σ_1, σ_0 σ_1 σ_0]` of `H_3(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.trace_e21p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.trace_e21p","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L237-L244","doc":"Rank trace of `e_{(2,1)}^p`: `tr(e_{(2,1)}^p) = 2` (2-dimensional `I = 1/2` nucleon sector). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.trace_e3p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.trace_e3p","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.lean#L232-L235","doc":"Rank trace of `e_{(3)}^p`: `tr(e_{(3)}^p) = 1` (1-dimensional `I = 3/2` decuplet sector). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace.trace_EFn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","